MPU6050 I²C Bring-Up Debug Summary

Objective: Read the WHO_AM_I register (0x75) from an MPU6050-6DoF sensor using STM32F446RE via I²C.

Problems Faced During Bring-Up

HAL_I2C_Mem_Read() failing / NO ACK from sensor

Initial code returned HAL_ERROR

Sensor did not acknowledge either 0x68 or 0x69

Initial wiring / pull-up mistakes

Added 4.7kΩ pull-ups from SDA/SCL to VCC (both 3.3V and 5V tested)

Incorrect pull-up voltage caused I²C logic level mismatch → no ACK

VCC confusion

MPU6050 breakout label: “I2C Logic / VCC 3–5V DC”

Feeding 3.3V sometimes underpowered board → no ACK

Feeding 5V OK, but pull-ups must remain at 3.3V

I2C address uncertainty

AD0 pin determines 7-bit address: 0x68 (AD0=GND) or 0x69 (AD0=VCC)

Tested both addresses; neither ACKed initially

CubeMX / STM32 configuration verification

PB6 = SCL (D15), PB7 = SDA (D14) — correct

HAL GPIO initialized correctly (Alternate Function Open-Drain, no internal pull-up)

Peripheral clock enabled → software configuration not the issue

Pull-ups already present on MPU6050 board

External pull-ups were redundant and in some cases interfered with logic levels

Root Causes Identified

Misalignment of pull-up voltage vs logic level

Misunderstanding of VCC vs I²C logic

Initial over-complication with external resistors

Electrical / bus stability (breadboard rails, wiring)

Final Known-Good Setup

VCC → 5V (Nucleo 5V pin)

GND → common GND

PB6 (D15) → SCL, PB7 (D14) → SDA

No external pull-ups (board has built-in 4.7kΩ to 3.3V)

I2C1, 100 kHz, GPIO mode AF_OD, no internal pull-up

Next Step: Run HAL_I2C_IsDeviceReady(&hi2c1, 0x68 << 1) — expected to return HAL_OK

31 Dec
The sensor has been recognised. The PB6 and the PB7 pins in the alternate mode have been mapped to the CN10-17th and the CN7-21th pin on the board
No pull resistors are added
Vcc used is 3.3V



