🧩 Why It Works (Key Lessons)

Nucleo pin names vs MCU pins matter
PB6/PB7 are routed to specific CN connectors, not just Arduino headers.

MPU6050 logic ≠ VCC label
Even though marked “3–5 V”, the I²C logic is 3.3 V.

Double pull-ups can break I²C
Adding external pull-ups on a board that already has them caused NO ACK.

NO ACK ≠ software bug
In this case, it was electrical + board routing, not HAL or code logic.
